<title>USA: GM says 23,340 workers idle.</title>
<headline>GM says 23,340 workers idle.</headline>
<dateline>WARREN, Mich. 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp said that as of 1600 EDT/2100 GMT, 23,340 of its workers in the U.S. and Mexico were idle as a result of the strike by the Canadian Auto Workers union that ended earlier this week.</p>
<p>The figure is unchanged from the previous update on Friday morning.</p>
<p>Canadian Auto Workers ratified a tentative deal on a new contract Tuesday and are heading back to their jobs in stages.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
